    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.nvim\n\n### Description\n\n`mini.nvim` is fantastic. First i was skeptical how one person can maintain a reasonable level of quality for so many sub-packages, but you proved yourself beyond my expectations. I want to support you, my Ukrainian brother. How can i do this?",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I sincerely thank you for the kind words and willingness for financial support!\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, at the moment GitHub Sponsors is not available in Ukraine. As it seems to be the easiest way enable support, I did not look any further yet. Maybe I should.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\n> .... how one person can maintain a reasonable level of quality for so many sub-packages.\r\n\r\nThe answer is mostly in the name and [general principles](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim?tab=readme-ov-file#general-principles). Most modules are already finished in terms of feature set. So for them only maintenance for breaking changes on Nightly (like latest `gra`/`grn` built-in mappings) and possibly reimplementing features (like the latest refactor of 'mini.statusline') is left.\r\n\r\nAnd writing new modules is usually fun for me, so there's that :)",
