            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "hey @echasnovski,\n\nhope you are doing great!\n\ntwo years have gone by, there is clearly no intent from the m$ side to enable gh sponsors for Ukrainian citizens\n\n> My main concern is that sponsoring should be made as easy for givers as it gets\n\nwith all due respect, i would strongly recommend you to abandon this concern. Unfortunately, it’s idealistic rather than pragmatic. Yes, it sucks that you cannot provide a zero-friction solution to sponsor you, but at the same time there are at least 13 people who are willing to support you and to my best knowledge none of them really care how exactly they have to do it. It makes my blood boil personally, especially given the sad circumstances your country is experiencing atm, but i’m inclined to work with what we have rather than holding out for perfection: you didn’t wait until someone—or even the neovim maintainers—made what you wanted, you just went ahead and created mini.nvim. I believe there is zero difference between this and the sponsoring situation, so in my opinion you every moral right to solve the problem in the exact same way!\n\nat the same time, i cannot say i’m happy that i haven’t been able to sponsor you just because m$ couldn’t care less. See, it’s been a bit of a weight on my conscience because i’ve been using your work for years without giving anything back and I would really love for that weight to be lifted\n\ni insist you revisit how we, your users, can support you man!\n\nkeep up the good work, you rock!",
